  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-30T15:53:17.137Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Toggle mute by pressing the trigger on the controller that has the quick menu open.\n\nThe action menu is inconvenient if deep in avatar 3.0 submenus, and the standard way requires 2 hands, needing to interrupt whatever is being done with hands (such as headpatting or driving or showing off avatars).\n\nAlso would eliminate requirement for dedicated input binding (especially troublesome on oculus, with very little button real estate).\n\nEdit: because of comments, i'm going to say again to be clear:  __these bindings via steamVR require you to use up an entire key in order do toggle mute__.  For people that use playspace mover and other such, there is no free buttons or keys without sacrificing something.  The entire point of this is to get rid of the need for using a whole extra input for it by being able to pull the trigger when the quick menu is out to toggle. Trigger on the hand that has the quick menu open is already a dud input that does nothing but make a sound.  (ps: for some people the hold input for steamvr is extremely laggy, like it destroys fps)",
